            <ArticleTitle>[Arthrography of the hand in an accident clinic (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>458-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>By 115 arthrographies of the wrist in patients with posttraumatic pain, the importance of the method for diagnosis in injured patients is discussed. It was possible to detect 29 cases with a lesion of the articular disc, 4 patients with ruptured radiocarpal joint and 3 cases with an injury of the distal radioulnar joint. The technique of filling the wrist is described and different manifestations of &quot;normal&quot; arthrogramms are exhibited.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
